xt{\\boldsymbol}f(x).$ \n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}+xy-2x+3y+5)=2x+y-2,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}+xy-2x+3y+5)=x+3 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({y}^{2}-x+4y+4)=-1,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({y}^{2}-x+4y+4)=2y+4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}2x+y-2 & x+3 \\\\ -1 & 2y+4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNext, we evaluate the Jacobian at the equilibrium ${x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ to get\n\n$$\n\\text{\\boldsymbol}{f}^{′}({x}^{∗})=[\\begin{aligned}2(1)+(-1)-2 & 1+3 \\\\ -1 & 2(-1)+4\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFinally, near the equilibrium, the nonlinear system is approximated by\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{aligned}]u,\n$$\n\nwhere the deviation vector is\n\n$$\nu=x-{x}^{∗}=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}x-1 \\\\ y+1\\end{aligned}].\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368185 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186368186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368185 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368185 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368185 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186368186 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368185 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "b8d25b9b-5373-5c00-8a36-5090fe82791f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368186 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368186 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368186 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "aae2533e-427c-5750-ae66-88d1e4378acc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186368187 #edb/ref 